1": 0.5639097740047392, "t": "9"}, {"y0": 0.2703488372441599, "y1": 0.28633720912211924, "x0": 0.588345864909892, "x1": 0.6165413536991307, "t": "27"}, {"y0": 0.27906976755190005, "y1": 0.29360465076205333, "x0": 0.43609022521820184, "x1": 0.4736842102705199, "t": "R="}, {"y0": 0.2892441858742798, "y1": 0.30087209290479, "x0": 0.4906015038761448, "x1": 0.501879698943404, "t": "1"}, {"y0": 0.2892441858742798, "y1": 0.30087209290479, "x0": 0.5187969925979494, "x1": 0.5300751876652087, "t": "4"}, {"y0": 0.2892441865042623, "y1": 0.30232558104660967, "x0": 0.5375939842258, "x1": 0.5695488721181852, "t": "16"}, {"y0": 0.2892441864835861, "y1": 0.30377906969373947, "x0": 0.5883458644889579, "x1": 0.6203007523813431, "t": "64"}, {"y0": 0.3023255815755552, "y1": 0.31831395345351454, "x0": 0.5018796966212445, "x1": 0.6296992481907856, "t": "525125]"}, {"y0": 0.3052325579673031, "y1": 0.3168604649978133, "x0": 0.48684210549714046, "x1": 0.5018796989201527, "t": "1"}, {"y0": 0.33575581398834586, "y1": 0.3517441858663053, "x0": 0.19360903852466702, "x1": 0.616541343457073, "t": "The absolute value of the product of Eigen values of R is"}, {"y0": 0.3938953488720669, "y1": 0.4098837207500261, "x0": 0.14097745693740935, "x1": 0.8740601475201629, "t": "Q.45 A certain processor deploys a single-level cache. The cache block size is 8 words and the"}, {"y0": 0.4096969695826417, "y1": 0.42606060594627804, "x0": 0.19360903757766698, "x1": 0.8740601466955157, "t": "word size is 4 bytes. The memory system uses a 60-MHz clock. To service a cache miss, the"}, {"y0": 0.42727272735884325, "y1": 0.441860464933565, "x0": 0.19172932323086536, "x1": 0.8740601333950748, "t": "memory controller first takes 1 cycle to accept the starting address of the block, it then takes"}, {"y0": 0.4430303031811188, "y1": 0.4607558142118362, "x0": 0.19360903294107554, "x1": 0.8740601420589242, "t": "3 cycles to fetch all the eight words of the block, and finally transmits the words of the"}, {"y0": 0.4593023257616018, "y1": 0.475290697639561, "x0": 0.19172932493669237, "x1": 0.8740601351009019, "t": "requested block at the rate of 1 word per cycle. The maximum bandwidth for the memory"}, {"y0": 0.47515151498991615, "y1": 0.48982558089771233, "x0": 0.1954887384141304, "x1": 0.8740601464856185, "t": "system when the program running on the processor issues a series of read operations is"}, {"y0": 0.48969696981826405, "y1": 0.5072727273940216, "x0": 0.23872180660134076, "x1": 0.39661653903775707, "t": "\u00d7 106 bytes/sec."}, {"y0": 0.5494186047067845, "y1": 0.5654545452816617, "x0": 0.14097745693740935, "x1": 0.8740601475201629, "t": "Q.46 Let T be a full binary tree with 8 leaves. (A full binary tree has every level full.) Suppose"}, {"y0": 0.5666666665256063, "y1": 0.5830303028892426, "x0": 0.193609026236815, "x1": 0.8740601353546639, "t": "two leaves a and b of T are chosen uniformly and independently at random. The expected"}, {"y0": 0.5812121211553959, "y1": 0.5988372091246268, "x0": 0.19172933074966217, "x1": 0.8740601409138716, "t": "value of the distance between a and b in T (i.e., the number of edges in the unique path"}, {"y0": 0.5987878786505044, "y1": 0.616363636226262, "x0": 0.1917293205845896, "x1": 0.5939849618402224, "t": "between a and b) is (rounded off to 2 decimal places)."}, {"y0": 0.6581818179184551, "y1": 0.6745454542820915, "x0": 0.14097744646479934, "x1": 0.8740601370475531, "t": "Q.47 Suppose Y is distributed uniformly in the open interval (1,6). The probability that the"}, {"y0": 0.6727272725797371, "y1": 0.690406976610092, "x0": 0.19360902735836888, "x1": 0.8740601364762175, "t": "polynomial 3x2 + 6xY + 3Y + 6 has only real roots is (rounded off to 1 decimal place)"}, {"y0": 0.7484848482495471, "y1": 0.7645348835528363, "x0": 0.1409774578101268, "x1": 0.8740601483928805, "t": "Q.48 Let E be the set of all bijections from {1,..., 5} to {1,..., 5}, where id denotes the identity"}, {"y0": 0.7659883720988111, "y1": 0.7819767439767703, "x0": 0.19360903871175217, "x1": 0.874060147829601, "t": "function, ie. id(j) = j,Vj. Let \u2022 denote composition on functions. For a string x ="}, {"y0": 0.7834302326220669, "y1": 0.7994186045000261, "x0": 0.19360902373935662, "x1": 0.5996240670877109, "t": "1X2. Xn EX\", n\u22650, letT(x) = x1\u00b0x2....0Xn."}, {"y0": 0.7963636364682091, "y1": 0.8139534881943943, "x0": 0.19360902786588777, "x1": 0.8740601369837365, "t": "Consider the language L = {x \u20ac 2*| n(x) = id}. The minimum number of states in any"}, {"y0": 0.8114995860663106, "y1": 0.8345741835117119, "x0": 0.1929293313537246, "x1": 0.34273807750028246, "t": "DFA accepting L is"}, {"y0": 0.9462209301330007, "y1": 0.9578488371635109, "x0": 0.12218045112592077, "x1": 0.14285714320365317, "t": "CS"}, {"y0": 0.9462209303560392, "y1": 0.9549418600509373, "x0": 0.8458646625293686, "x1": 0.8759398493753933, "t": "11/15"}]